    "alert_id": "P005_TDF_FATIGUE_SYMPTOM",
    "title": "Fatigue may signal TDF-related toxicity",
    "message": "Guidelines list exhaustion or extreme fatigue as a presenting sign of TDF toxicity including lactic acidosis and Fanconi syndrome. The patient reports mild fatigue over 2 months, attributed to work schedule. While the self-attribution and mild nature argue against drug toxicity, the concurrent renal decline (creatinine 1.4, eGFR 52) and proteinuria increase concern. Lactic acidosis and Fanconi syndrome are serious TDF complications that require evaluation. Alternative explanations such as anaemia (Hb 12.8, borderline low-normal) should also be assessed.",
    "issue_type": "toxicity",
    "severity": "moderate",
    "recommended_action": "Evaluate fatigue with LFTs, RFTs, and lactate if clinically indicated. Consider TDF-related toxicity in differential diagnosis.",
